-- title:
--   Residue of U_q as Frobenius trace on inertia coinvariants
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology) with finite residue field, let $p \neq 2$ be a prime with $p \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual representation over $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}$: a rank-two $k$-space $V$ with a homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ trivial on the fixator of a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, assumed absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to $\overline{k}$). Let $M \geq 1$ and let $S_0$ be a finite set of naturals containing no prime divisor of $M$; assume $p^2 \nmid M$, that for every prime $q \neq p$ with $q \mid M$, $q^2 \nmid M$ the representation $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ and has $\bar\rho(\tau)$ of characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ for every $\tau$ in inertia at every place over $q$, and that if $p \mid M$ then $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$ (at each place over $p$ a free rank-one submodule spanned by a basis vector, stable under the decomposition group, containing $(\bar\rho(\tau)-1)V$ for $\tau$ inertial). Assume $\mathrm{CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure}\ M\ 2$. On $H^1 := \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_0(M)^{\mathrm{ab}}, \mathcal{O})$ the operators $\mathrm{opFamily}\,M\,\top\,S_0\,\mathcal{O}$ indexed by the generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S_0$, $\ell \nmid M$), $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q \mid M$) and $\langle d\rangle$ ($d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$) are assumed to commute pairwise. Let $\bar\theta$ assign a scalar in $k$ to each generator, such that for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \neq p$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $P$ for $\ell$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \bar\theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Let $Sp$ be an idempotent splitting of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}}(H^1)$ generated by these operators (a complete orthogonal family of idempotents $e_i$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting the maximal ideals, $e_i \in \mathfrak{m}_j$ exactly for $i \neq j$), let $i_0$ be an index, and let $\pi_k$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map from the corner ring at $i_0$ to $k$ sending the corner image of each generator's operator to $\bar\theta$ of that generator. Assume the corner submodule $e_{i_0} \cdot H^1$ is non-zero, and that $\bar\theta(U_p) \neq 0$ whenever $p \mid M$. Then for every prime $q \mid M$ with $q^2 \nmid M$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$, every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $P$ for $q$, and every $k$-linear endomorphism $E$ of the inertia coinvariants $V / \sum_{\tau \in I_P} \mathrm{im}(\bar\rho(\tau)-1)$ satisfying $E(\bar v) = \overline{\bar\rho(\sigma)v}$ for all $v \in V$, one has $\bar\theta(U_q) = \mathrm{tr}(E)$.
--
--   This is local-global compatibility at a prime exactly dividing the level, in residual form: for an eigensystem occurring in the $\bar\rho$-congruent local factor of the weight-two cohomology of $\Gamma_0(M)$, the $U_q$-eigenvalue is the trace of Frobenius on the inertia coinvariants of $\bar\rho$, covering both the case $q \neq p$ with unipotent ramified inertia and the ordinary case $q = p$. It feeds the local analysis of the Hecke algebra at such primes, being used by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algEquiv_sigmaCornerRing_auxLevel`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algEquiv_sigmaCornerRing_auxLevel) and [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_corner_smul_eq_heckeT_residueChar_gammaZero`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_corner_smul_eq_heckeT_residueChar_gammaZero).
